# Agent Onboarding — First Steps for Every New Session

When starting a new conversation in this repo, complete these steps **before** doing any other work.

## 1. Read `AGENTS.md`

This workspace is a local proof of concept: Concrete Device ID → race history → one car → themed HTML logbook.

## 2. Read the active plan

Read [`Documents/plans/20260924_project-setup.plan.md`](../../Documents/plans/20260924_project-setup.plan.md).

## 3. Check `Documents/todo.md`

## 4. Sister-repo context

All **read-only** unless the user scopes a dedicated PR session:

- `~/Cursor Projects/Project Startup Best Practices/`
- `~/Cursor Projects/NHRA Marketing/` — brand and guardrails
- `~/Cursor Projects/Slack Integratation Test/` — bot token for read-only Slack
- `~/git/unity/apps/nhra/` — analytics event fields
- `~/git/services/ai-env/`

## 5. Phase status

Local server only. No Jira ID. No git repo required yet. Do not deploy, do not post to Slack, and do not invent car history.

## Then proceed

Once you have this context, complete the onboarding silently (don't narrate each step) and address the user's request.
